    <description>
      <para>The Auxiliary Power Unit (APU) is a small gas-turbine unit installed in the tailcone that supplies electrical power and bleed air when the main engines are not running. Refer to <graphicRef infoEntityIdent="ICN-MERM10012A00-001"/> for a general arrangement diagram.</para>
      <para>For the inlet filter remove procedure, see <dmRef><dmRefIdent><dmCode modelIdentCode="MERM100" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="049" subSystemCode="0" subSubSystemCode="0" assyCode="00AA" disassyCode="00" disassyCodeVariant="A" infoCode="040" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="A"/></dmRefIdent></dmRef>. For the install procedure, see <dmRef><dmRefIdent><dmCode modelIdentCode="MERM100" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="049" subSystemCode="0" subSubSystemCode="0" assyCode="00AA" disassyCode="00" disassyCodeVariant="A" infoCode="041" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="A"/></dmRefIdent></dmRef>.</para>
